  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The strongest H-bond is $\\mathrm{F}-\\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{F}$ because in this case, a hydrogen is bonded to a most. electronegative atom i.e. fluorine. In all other options, hydrogen is bonded to oxygen and sulphur that are less electronegative atom than fluorine.\r\nThe correct electronegativity order of elements are as follows: $\\mathrm{F}>\\mathrm{O}>\\mathrm{S}$",
    "image": null
  },
